Parse content-addressed, deferred, impure and dynamic derivations instead
of emitting DerivationParseError "string".

nix-derivation 1.1.3 only accepts input-addressed ATerm outputs
("out","/nix/store/…","",""): its filepath parser rejects the empty path
used by floating CA outputs ("out","","r:sha256",""), deferred outputs
("out","","","") and impure outputs ("out","","r:sha256","impure"), and it
does not know DrvWithVersion("xp-dyn-drv",…) nor the dynamic inputDrvs node
form. Any such .drv (e.g. the llvm runtimes CA build) therefore failed with

  nix-output-monitor error: DerivationParseError "string"

This vendors a tolerant in-tree ATerm parser (NOM.Derivation) that keeps
the known output path as Maybe FilePath — Nothing for floating CA,
deferred and impure outputs, which are then skipped in insertDerivation
since there is no store path to wait for — and flattens dynamic inputDrvs
nodes. The nix-derivation dependency is dropped. Upstream issues:
maralorn/nix-output-monitor#167,
Gabriella439/Haskell-Nix-Derivation-Library#28.

